Not compared (cargo packaging output, never accepted as a build target):
  Cargo.toml: normalized by cargo publish; gpui-pre also renames the package and its gpui dependencies to gpui-pre-* and adds [package.metadata.gpui-pre]
  Cargo.toml.orig: the publisher's manifest before normalization; Cargo never reads it
  Cargo.lock: generated by cargo package for the crate alone; ignored when the crate is a dependency
  .cargo_vcs_info.json: VCS note written by cargo package; metadata only (gpui-pre ships none)
Upstream normalization:
  symlinks: Zed tracks LICENSE-* as git symlinks; cargo packages the target's content, so the crate file is compared with the target blob
  nested packages: files below a subdirectory with its own Cargo.toml belong to another package and are left out by cargo package (as Zed's derive_refineable and gpui_web/examples/hello_web)
